-+# Exo Academic Platform — Phase 4.1 Engineering Audit Report
-+
-+**Repository:** `JemistryMC/study-hub`  
-+**Target Branch:** `fix/phase-4-1-account-isolation` (branched from `main`)  
-+**Scope:** Critical Account Isolation, Async Sync Race Conditions, IndexedDB Transaction Integrity & Real Chromium E2E Verification
-+
-+---
-+
-+## 1. Executive Summary of Resolved Vulnerabilities & Defects
-+
-+All P0 and P1 defects identified in the Phase 4.1 engineering review have been fixed directly in production code (`index.html`), verified across unit/regression suites (`run_verification_tests.js`, `run_comprehensive_verification.js`, `test_phase3_cross_account_isolation.js`, `test_phase4_regressions.js`), and validated in real Headless Chromium with real browser `IndexedDB` (`WorkspaceMediaStore` v4) via `test_phase4_1_chromium_e2e.js`.
-+
-+---
-+
-+## 2. Detailed Root-Cause & Remediation Matrix
-+
-+### 2.1 P0 — Account Switch Race Conditions Across Async Sync & Restore Operations
-+- **Root Cause:** `syncWorkspaceOnLogin()`, `pullWorkspaceFromCloud()`, `pullWorkspaceFromCloudIfNewer()`, `applyCloudWorkspacePayload()`, `mergeAndApplyCloudConflict()`, `pushWorkspaceToCloud()`, `restoreAllAnnotationsMapToDB()`, and `getAllAnnotationsMapFromDB()` relied on mutable global `currentCloudUser` across `await` boundaries without binding a session epoch/generation. If Account A initiated a network pull or conflict merge and the user switched to Account B while awaiting network/IndexedDB I/O, Account A's late response would overwrite Account B's workspace state, `inMemoryAnnotationsCache`, and `IndexedDB` records.
-+- **Affected Functions & Line Numbers (`index.html`):**
-+  - `bumpAccountSessionGeneration()` (`index.html:19303`)
-+  - `createAccountOperationContext()` (`index.html:19335`)
-+  - `resolveAccountOperationContext()` (`index.html:19362`)
-+  - `handleAuthSessionChange()` (`index.html:26071`)
-+  - `getAllAnnotationsMapFromDB()` (`index.html:28981`)
-+  - `restoreAllAnnotationsMapToDB()` (`index.html:29107`)
-+  - `mergeAndApplyCloudConflict()` (`index.html:29289`)
-+  - `pushWorkspaceToCloud()` (`index.html:29541`)
-+  - `applyCloudWorkspacePayload()` (`index.html:29784`)
-+  - `pullWorkspaceFromCloud()` (`index.html:29929`)
-+  - `syncWorkspaceOnLogin()` (`index.html:29969`)
-+  - `pullWorkspaceFromCloudIfNewer()` (`index.html:30081`)
-+- **Remediation:**
-+  - Introduced an immutable `AccountOperationContext` (`{ uid, sanitizedUid, generation, sessionEpoch, authorized, ok, error, isCurrent() }`) backed by a monotonically increasing `currentSessionGeneration` counter incremented on every account switch.
-+  - Bound `opCtx` at the entry of every async workflow and verified `opCtx.isCurrent()` before and after every `await` boundary. Stale contexts immediately abort (`{ status: 'aborted', reason: 'account_switched' }`) before touching global state, `localStorage`, caches, or `IndexedDB`.
-+- **Linked Tests & Results:**
-+  - `test_phase4_1_chromium_e2e.js` — **Test B (B.1–B.3)** & **Test C (C.1–C.4)**: **PASSED**
-+  - `test_phase4_regressions.js` — **Test 3**: **PASSED**
-+
